    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "Run the full suite with `make test` (the Makefile runs `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`). `./tools/test` does not exist in this repo. `python -m unittest discover tests` without PYTHONPATH=src fails to import the package because of the src layout.",
    "helpful": 5,
    "harmful": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "`cli.main(argv)` returns the exit code: 0 for success, 1 for a failed check (e.g. over budget), 2 for bad input. New commands and options get a test in `tests/test_cli.py` that calls `cli.main` and checks the returned code.",
    "helpful": 3,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "Write files only with repo-relative paths. The sandbox blocks writes outside the workspace (e.g. /tmp/...), so use paths like CHANGELOG.md or release/X.sha256.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "When the user asks to cut or release a tally version (e.g. 'cut the 0.5.0 release'), load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps.",
